## Atari 2600 for MEGA65
##
## Core specific constraints
##
## This machine is based on Atari2600_MiSTer (https://github.com/MiSTer-devel/Atari2600_MiSTer)
## Powered by MiSTer2MEGA65
## Licensed under GPL v3


## Name Autogenerated Clocks
## Important: Using them in subsequent statements, e.g. clock dividers requires that they
## have been named/defined here before
## otherwise Vivado does not find the pins)
create_generated_clock -name main_clk [get_pins CORE/clk_gen/i_clk_main/CLKOUT0]

## cpu_clk: the Atari's 3.579545 MHz colour clock. It is main_clk (57.27 MHz) passed through a
## BUFGCE that lets exactly one of 16 pulses through (see clk.vhd): it rises on main_clk edge 1,
## falls on edge 2 and rises again on edge 33, i.e. a period of 16 main_clk periods.
create_generated_clock -name cpu_clk -source [get_pins CORE/clk_gen/cpu_clk_bufgce/I] \
   -edges {1 2 33} [get_pins CORE/clk_gen/cpu_clk_bufgce/O]

## main_clk and cpu_clk come from the same MMCM output and the same kind of global buffer, so
## all transfers between them (TIA colour table, video sampling, controls) are timed normally.
## The cartridge loader crosses from qnice_clk with xpm_cdc_array_single, which brings its own
## constraints; the cartridge RAM is only written while the Atari is held in reset.
